{"id":"03dd415c-387c-4502-b838-a9d52c0619c0","object":"chat.completion","created":1785030678,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    if n <= 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Need at least 2 nodes for MST\\\")\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u == v:\\n            continue\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mutual = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mutual, u, v))\\n    edges.sort()\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        xr, yr = find(x), find(y)\\n        if xr == yr:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[xr] < rank[yr]:\\n            parent[xr] = yr\\n        elif rank[xr] > rank[yr]:\\n            parent[yr] = xr\\n        else:\\n            parent[yr] = xr\\n            rank[xr] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    edges_used = 0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            edges_used += 1\\n            if edges_used == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if edges_used != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected, cannot compute MST\\\")\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that computes MST based on mutual reachability. Steps:\n\n1. Input: case has nodes (list of strings), core_distance (dict node->float), distances (list of [nodeA, nodeB, dist] triples). distances are symmetric? Probably each pair appears only once. We'll handle symmetric.\n\n2. For each pair (u,v) with distance d, compute mutual_reachability = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d). Add edge.\n\n3. Build graph with all nodes. Need to ensure connectivity? The problem says \"Reject disconnected inputs\". So after constructing edges, if the graph is disconnected, raise ValueError.\n\n4. Compute MST using Kruskal's algorithm. Sort edges by weight (mutual reachability), and as tie-breaker by u then v (lexicographic order of the two node identifiers, canonicalized undirected endpoints). We need stable deterministic ordering. Since u and v are strings, we can sort tuple (weight, u, v) where u < v lexicographically.\n\n5. Union-Find (Disjoint Set Union) with path compression and union by rank. Add edges until we have n-1 edges. If after processing all edges we don't have n-1 edges, graph disconnected -> ValueError.\n\n6. Return object: {\"mst_edges\": list of [u, v, weight], \"total_weight\": sum of weights}.\n\n7. Ensure no mutation of case.\n\n8. Use only standard library.\n\nWrite function solve(case).\n\nImplementation details:\n\n- Validate fields exist? Not strictly required but we can check presence of nodes, core_distance, distances. But the contract says \"Do not expect case_id, seed...\". We'll just assume correct structure.\n\n- Canonicalize undirected endpoints: if u > v, swap.\n\n- Sorting: we can sort edges list of tuples (weight, u, v) with u<v sorted, then for tie-breaking, Python's default tuple sorting works: first weight, then compared as strings lexicographically.\n\n- Union-Find: dictionary parent, rank.\n\n- Return serializable data.\n\nEdge case: empty nodes? Not in fixtures.\n\nWrite code.\n\nAlso, note that distances list may have each pair once. We'll iterate over distances.\n\nNow produce JSON output with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nMake sure to escape newlines, quotes, backslashes. Use json.dumps on the Python source string to proper JSON string.\n\nImplementation code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    core = case['core_distance']\n    distances = case['distances']\n    n = len(nodes)\n    if n <= 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Need at least 2 nodes for MST\")\n    # Build edges with mutual reachability\n    edges = []\n    for u, v, d in distances:\n        if u == v:\n            continue\n        if u > v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        mutual = max(core[u], core[v], d)\n        edges.append((mutual, u, v))\n    # Sort edges: weight, then u, then v (u,v already canonicalized)\n    edges.sort()\n    # Union-Find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    def union(x, y):\n        xr, yr = find(x), find(y)\n        if xr == yr:\n            return False\n        if rank[xr] < rank[yr]:\n            parent[xr] = yr\n        elif rank[xr] > rank[yr]:\n            parent[yr] = xr\n        else:\n            parent[yr] = xr\n            rank[xr] += 1\n        return True\n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    edges_used = 0\n    for w, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\n            total_weight += w\n            edges_used += 1\n            if edges_used == n - 1:\n                break\n    if edges_used != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected, cannot compute MST\")\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\n```\n\nTest with given fixtures? Not now.\n\nNow produce final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2021,"completion_tokens":1423,"total_tokens":3444,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":966},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":101},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}